      metric: 'Direct human illness and duration, harmful-event composition, current multi-taxon mortality, affected regional area and duration of demonstrated consequences.',
      earlyBaseline: 'The monitoring-adjusted 1985–2018 marine record is retained as historical context. It shows regional increases and decreases but no statistically significant uniform global trend after monitoring effort is considered.',
      recentState: `The global assessment records ${harmfulAlgalBloomsReference.endpoints.humanConsequences.ciguateraAnnualAffectedPeople.lower.toLocaleString('en-US')}–${harmfulAlgalBloomsReference.endpoints.humanConsequences.ciguateraAnnualAffectedPeople.upper.toLocaleString('en-US')} people affected by ciguatera annually. The FAO/WHO assessment reports that at least ${harmfulAlgalBloomsReference.endpoints.humanConsequences.chronicSymptomShareLowerBoundPercent}% may have symptoms beyond three months.`,
