      reach: { lower: 1, central: 2, upper: 3, sourceAnchored: false, basis: `Harmful events occur across the assessed global marine regions and the current event covered about ${harmfulAlgalBloomsReference.endpoints.currentEcosystemEvent.affectedAreaApproximateKm2.toLocaleString('en-US')} km². Neither monitored regions nor event area supplies the affected share of global aquatic ecosystem distributions, so multi-region level 2 is central with levels 1–3.` },
      persistence: { lower: 1, central: 2, upper: 3, sourceAnchored: false, basis: `The current bloom and mortality persisted for more than ${harmfulAlgalBloomsReference.endpoints.currentEcosystemEvent.durationMonthsLowerBound} months, directly crossing the one-year threshold and supporting level 2 as a consequence-duration lower bound. Global ecological recovery is unmeasured, so shorter events and multi-year population recovery retain levels 1–3.` },
