      reach: 'People affected and the share of relevant aquatic ecosystem distributions with demonstrated condition loss. Monitored regions, database records and the area of one regional event establish evidence scope only.',
      persistence: 'Duration or recovery of the human or ecological consequence. Symptom duration and current event duration are admitted; database span and publication age are excluded.',
      nonDoubleCounting: 'Ciguatera counts enter human reach once. Poisoning type enters human severity, chronic symptoms enter human persistence, current mortality enters ecosystem severity and the regional event duration bounds ecosystem persistence. The 9,503 reports, 7% event share, 34-year record and downstream fishery or water-service nodes do not add points.',
