    finding: 'Changed from D 7.0, C–E range, to C 5.5, B–D range, with confidence C retained. The old review treated monitoring geography as reach, the 7% event share as ecosystem harm and the 34-year database span as persistence. Current ingestion instead assigns illness, reach, symptom duration, regional mortality and event duration to separate axes and leaves the missing worldwide ecosystem denominator explicit.',
