      metric: 'Mapped loss, gain and degradation of mangroves, seagrasses and salt marshes relative to each habitat product’s own distribution.',
      earlyBaseline: 'Global Mangrove Watch supplies the longest compatible mapped record, beginning in 1985 with a documented pre-2000 imagery caveat. The other habitats begin later and retain their source-native baselines.',
      recentState: `From 2016–2025, Global Mangrove Watch maps ${blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.endpoints.mangrove.grossLossHa.toLocaleString('en-US')} ha of gross loss, ${blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.endpoints.mangrove.grossLossPctOfBaseline}% of the 2016 baseline, alongside ${blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.endpoints.mangrove.grossGainPctOfBaseline}% gross gain and ${blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.endpoints.mangrove.netChangePctOfBaseline}% net change.`,
      currentState: `The 2026 global seagrass study maps ${blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.endpoints.seagrass.publishedMappedExtentKm2.toLocaleString('en-US')} km² and reports ${blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.endpoints.seagrass.publishedLossKm2.toLocaleString('en-US')} km² (${blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.endpoints.seagrass.publishedLossPct}%) lost plus ${blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.endpoints.seagrass.publishedDenseToSparseDegradationKm2.toLocaleString('en-US')} km² (${blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.endpoints.seagrass.publishedDenseToSparseDegradationPct}%) degraded from dense to sparse cover between its paired periods.`,
      fullRecordTrend: 'Blue-carbon habitat change is heterogeneous. Gross local loss persists even where gains elsewhere produce a stable or positive net total. The review therefore records loss, gain and degradation separately and does not claim uniform worldwide decline.',
      observedImpact: 'Mapped conversion to non-habitat directly establishes loss of the defining local ecosystem state. Dense-to-sparse seagrass change establishes degradation. Carbon emissions and reduced burial are reported consequences but are not reused as habitat area, harmed people or an additional score.',
      attribution: 'The mapping products detect habitat change but do not assign every lost pixel to climate change or one cause. The node assesses observed habitat loss itself and does not import causal shares from upstream nodes.',
      limitations: 'No compatible current global source counts unique people experiencing attributable loss of fisheries, shoreline protection, water quality or another essential service. Recovery duration is not measured globally, and no shared denominator combines all blue-carbon habitats.',
      evidenceReferences: Object.values(blueCarbonHabitatLossReference.sources).map(source => source.id),
