      recentState: `IMBIE reports ${iceSheetMassLossReference.endpoints.physicalState.combinedIceLoss1979To2023Gt.central.toLocaleString('en-US')} ± ${iceSheetMassLossReference.endpoints.physicalState.combinedIceLoss1979To2023Gt.uncertaintyPlusMinus} Gt of combined loss over 1979-2023, equivalent to ${iceSheetMassLossReference.endpoints.physicalState.combinedGlobalMeanSeaLevelContribution1979To2023Mm.central} ± ${iceSheetMassLossReference.endpoints.physicalState.combinedGlobalMeanSeaLevelContribution1979To2023Mm.uncertaintyPlusMinus} mm of global mean sea-level rise.`,
      currentState: `During 2020-2023 Greenland lost ${iceSheetMassLossReference.endpoints.physicalState.greenlandLoss2020To2023GtPerYear.central} ± ${iceSheetMassLossReference.endpoints.physicalState.greenlandLoss2020To2023GtPerYear.uncertaintyPlusMinus} Gt per year. Antarctica continued to lose mass overall, with recent East Antarctic snowfall partly offsetting sustained West Antarctic dynamic loss.`,
