    finding: 'Replaced evidence ending in 2016 with a 2000–2024 global field synthesis, a two-model factual-versus-detrended-climate check and checksum-pinned regional consequence data. The candidate remains C 5.9 with a B–D range and confidence C: physical attribution and direct regional harm are stronger, while global terminal-harm denominators and recovery evidence remain unresolved and downstream carbon, thermokarst, erosion and infrastructure scores are excluded.',
