      reach: { lower: 1, central: 2, upper: 2, basis: 'USGS and the Yukon-Kuskokwim study establish substantial regional coastal change. Coastline length, habitat area, regional population and the number of communities are not a compatible affected share of the global coastal-permafrost ecosystem distribution, retaining levels 1–2.' },
      persistence: { lower: 3, central: 4, upper: 4, basis: 'Eroded coastal land and collapsed permafrost terrain can be effectively permanent locally. The studies do not provide a recovery-time distribution for affected ecosystems, so levels 3–4 remain.' },
